ation in Chinese Medicine (CME) for Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioners</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cmchk.org.hk/cmp/eng/idx_rcmp04.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>The Chinese Medicine Council of Hong Kong</collab></person-group><article-title>CME Scopes, Requirements and Points Assessment System of CME Programes</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cmchk.org.hk/cmp/pdf/AnnexD_e.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Hong Kong SAR Legislative Council Discussion</collab></person-group><article-title>Professional Development for Chinese Medicine Graduates</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.legco.gov.hk/yr04-05/english/counmtg/hansard/cm1027ti-translate-e.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Hong Kong SAR Legislative Council Motion</collab></person-group><article-title>Overall Development of Chinese medicine practitioners</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.legco.gov.hk/yr04-05/english/counmtg/hansard/cm1202ti-translate-e.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Health, Welfare and Food Bureau and the Hospital Authority of the Hong Kong SAR Government</collab></person-group><article-title>The future direction for the development of traditional Chinese medicine services in the public sector</article-title><source>Discussion paper</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Hong Kong: The Legislative Council</publisher-name><comment>Report No.: CB(2)1748/04-05(05)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Wen Wei Po Daily News</collab></person-group><article-title>Unemployment rates remain high for local TCM graduates</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://trans.wenweipo.com/gb/paper.wenweipo.com/2007/08/29/HK0708290024.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>ZZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Liang</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name></person-group><source>Wen ding Zhong yi : Jin da qing nian Zhong yi de si kao (Some Thoughts by HKBU TCM Graduates). 1st ed</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Hong Kong: Tian yao she ji yin wu gong si</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>The Sun Daily News</collab></person-group><article-title>Job Searching for TCM Graduates Remains Difficult</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://the-sun.on.cc/channels/news/20070829/20070829023534_0000.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mays</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Pope</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rigour and qualitative research</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1995</year><volume>311</volume><fpage>109</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7613363</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knodel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Morgan DL</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The Design and Analysis of Focus Group Studies: A Practical Approach</article-title><source>Successful Focus Groups: Advancing the State of the Art</source><year>1993</year><edition>1</edition><publisher-name>London: Sage Publications</publi